 "source_notes": "All values from Bowen National Research, '2024 Housing Supply Gap Analysis, State of North Carolina', read from the City of Hendersonville mirror of the full PDF (ncchamber.com URL was blocked in this session). No news/secondary sources used. GAPS: table 'Housing Gaps by Tenure and County - State of North Carolina (2024 to 2029)' (pp. II-15 to II-17), columns 'Total Rental Gap', 'Total For-Sale Gap', 'Total Gap', each with 'Share of State' and 'Gap to Renter/Owner/Total Households Ratio' (stored as *_gap_to_*_hh_pct). HOUSEHOLDS: table 'Total Households' (pp. III-23 to III-24), columns '2024 Estimated', '2029 Projected', 'Change 2024-2029' (number, percent) -> hh_growth_pct is the printed percent. rental_gap_by_ami: 'Overall Rental Housing Gaps - State of North Carolina (2024 to 2029)' (pp. V-5 to V-7), columns by percent of Area Median Income <30%, 31%-50%, 51%-80%, 81%-120%, 121%-150%, 151%+; cross-checked against Addendum A rows 'Total Rental Housing Gaps'. forsale_gap_by_price: the report gives the for-sale gap by AMI band, not by fixed price point: 'Overall For-Sale Housing Gaps' (pp. V-13 to V-15) = by_ami; price_range_for_ami_band is the county-specific 'Price Range' row from Addendum A '[COUNTY] COUNTY Housing Gap Estimates by Income (2024 to 2029)' (pp. A-5 to A-9), i.e. the home price affordable to each band. Price ranges differ by county. Gaston's first band printed/extracted without the '≤' sign; '≤' added here. multifamily_vacancy_pct: 'Surveyed Multifamily Rental Housing Supply by County' (pp. IV-4 to IV-6), column 'Overall Vacancy Rate' (all surveyed market-rate + Tax Credit + government-subsidized projects; physical vacancies only). null = 0 projects surveyed in that county (printed '-'), NOT a 0% rate. Small samples in some counties (e.g. Hertford 1 project/48 units, Franklin 2 projects). forsale_availability_pct and median_list_price: 'Available For-Sale Housing by County (As of Early July 2024)' (pp. IV-36 to IV-38), columns 'Availability Rate' ('the comparison of available units to overall owner-occupied housing supply') and 'Median List Price'. Validation: every county read twice with differently worded extractions; rental+forsale=total, AMI bands sum to tenure totals, and printed growth % matches 2024/2029 households for all 25.",
